  "title": "Simple Celery and Onion Base",
  "blurb": "A gentle, savoury base of softened celery and onion cooked in butter. Use it as a foundation for soups, stews, or stir through pasta.",
  "steps": [
    "Melt the butter in a wide frying pan over a medium heat.",
    "Add the celery and onion, then stir to coat everything in the butter.",
    "Cook gently for 15 to 20 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables are very soft and translucent but not browned.",
    "Season with the salt and black pepper, stir through, then taste and adjust if needed.",
    "Use immediately as a base for other dishes, or cool and store in the fridge for up to three days."
